  <h2 id="receipt-scanning">Receipt Scanning Accuracy</h2>

  <p>
    Receipt scanning uses OCR (Optical Character Recognition) to extract data. Quality varies:
  </p>

  <h3>Best Receipt Scanning</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Expensify SmartScan:</strong> Human-verified for accuracy, handles handwritten receipts</li>
    <li><strong>Shoeboxed:</strong> Optional human verification, excellent for faded receipts</li>
    <li><strong>Rydoo:</strong> AI-powered, handles multiple languages well</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Tips for Better Scans</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Photograph in good lighting with receipt flat</li>
    <li>Capture the entire receipt including date and total</li>
    <li>Scan immediately—thermal paper fades quickly</li>
    <li>Add notes for unclear items while you remember</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="multi-currency">Multi-Currency for Nomads</h2>

  <p>
    Digital nomads deal with multiple currencies constantly. The best expense apps handle this:
  </p>

  <h3>Automatic Currency Conversion</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Expensify:</strong> Converts at date-of-purchase exchange rate</li>
    <li><strong>Rydoo:</strong> Real-time rates with automatic conversion</li>
    <li><strong>Wave:</strong> Multi-currency accounts and transactions</li>
    <li><strong>YNAB:</strong> Multi-currency budgets and tracking</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Tax Reporting in Home Currency</h3>
  <p>
    You'll need to report all income and expenses in your home currency for taxes. Make sure
    your app can export reports in a single currency with proper exchange rate documentation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="integrations">Accounting Software Integrations</h2>

  <p>
    Your expense tracker should sync with your accounting software to avoid double entry:
  </p>

  <h3>QuickBooks Integration</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Expensify, Zoho Expense, Shoeboxed all sync directly</li>
    <li>QuickBooks Self-Employed is built-in</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Xero Integration</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Expensify, Zoho Expense, Rydoo all integrate</li>
    <li>Receipt Bank (Dext) is popular with Xero users</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>FreshBooks Integration</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Built-in expense tracking is solid</li>
    <li>Expensify integration available</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <FAQSection faqs={faqData}/>

  <h2>Our Recommendations</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Best Overall:</strong> Expensify — Best receipt scanning, multi-currency, integrations</li>
    <li><strong>Best for Tax:</strong> QuickBooks Self-Employed — Expense tracking + tax estimates</li>
    <li><strong>Best Free:</strong> Wave — Full features at no cost</li>
    <li><strong>Best for Nomads:</strong> Rydoo — Multi-currency, travel-focused, per diems</li>
    <li><strong>Best for Budgeting:</strong> YNAB — Control spending, not just track it</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Start tracking today. Every expense you capture is a potential tax deduction—the savings
    compound throughout the year.
  </p>

